{"description":"Build a statusline for the lets plugin (inspired by claude-watch reference/claude-watch/). Show: active task + status, git branch, beads stats (open/blocked/wip), context window usage, dolt sync status.

Implementation: add statusLine config to PROJECT-SCOPED .claude/settings.json (not user ~/.claude/). This way it activates only in projects using the lets plugin. Scripts live in hooks/ directory of the plugin.

Reference implementation uses PreToolUse + Stop hooks to keep data fresh, shell scripts + jq, cached in /tmp (we use .lets/cache/). Adapt for lets plugin - show workflow-relevant info instead of just usage stats."}
